{\*\ftnsep\chftnsep}\pgndec\pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af10\afs48\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\sb240\sa120\keepn\f3\fs48\b\dbch\af7\ql\sb240\sa120\ltrpar{\loch
busyback-locate}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af8\loch
busyback-locate}{\loch
 is a high-performance CLI tool for OpenWrt. It searches through historical }{\loch
busyback }{\loch
backup snapshots for specific files or directories and displays }{\loch\b\loch
only real changes}{\loch
 (unique versions). Unchanged backups that were linked via hard links (}{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af8\loch
rsync --link-dest}{\loch
) are automatically filtered out to save time and cognitive load.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af10\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\sb200\sa120\ltrpar{\loch
How It Works}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
To minimize CPU load on your router and reduce disk thrashing on your backup drive, the tool uses a fast, }{\loch
compressed }{\loch\b\loch
index-based approach}{\loch
:}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain  1.\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch\b\loch
Index Generation & Compression (During Backup): }{\rtlch\ab0 \ltrch\loch\b0\loch
After every successful backup run, the main script creates a flat metadata list of every single backed-up item (storing inode, size, type, and relative path). This list is immediately compressed using }{\rtlch\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs15\rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af8\b0\loch
gzip}{\rtlch\ab0 \ltrch\loch\b0\loch
 and saved as }{\rtlch\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs15\rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af8\b0\loch
index.gz}{\rtlch\ab0 \ltrch\loch\b0\loch
 inside the snapshot directory, drastically reducing the storage footprint on the backup medium.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain  2.\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch\b\loch
Smart Data Filtering (During Search):}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af5 \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\f5\dbch\af5 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl1\ls2 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx1418\fi-283\li1418\lin1418\ltrpar{\loch\b\loch
Stream Decompression:}{\loch
 When searching, }{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af8\loch
busyback-locate}{\loch
 streams the contents of }{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af8\loch
index.gz}{\loch
 directly into memory using }{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af8\loch
zcat}{\loch
, ensuring lightning-fast text searches without extracting files to the disk.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af5 \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\f5\dbch\af5 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl1\ls2 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx1418\fi-283\li1418\lin1418\ltrpar{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
Files & Symlinks: }{\loch
The tool checks the physical inode number on the filesystem. If the inode in a newer snapshot matches one from a previous snapshot, it is identified as a hard link (no data changed) and skipped.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af5 \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\f5\dbch\af5 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl1\ls2 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx1418\fi-283\li1418\lin1418\ltrpar{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
Directories:}{\loch
 Because Linux filesystems do not allow hard-linking directories, }{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af8\loch
busyback-locate}{\loch
 tracks them using a unique fingerprint based on their path and directory size (which only changes under Linux when files inside that specific directory are added or deleted).}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af10\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\sb200\sa120\ltrpar{\loch
Usage}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
The tool requires two arguments: the name of the }{\loch\b\loch
vault}{\loch
 (backup target directory) and a }{\loch\b\loch
search pattern}{\loch
 (filename, partial name, or path fragment).}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af10\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\sb140\sa120\keepn\f3\fs28\b\dbch\af7\ql\sb140\sa120\ltrpar{\loch
Syntax}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\fi0\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ltrpar{\loch
Bash}
\par \pard\plain \s23\rtlch\af4\afs20 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sb0\sa0\f4\fs20\dbch\af8\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af8\loch
busyback-locate <vault_name> <search_pattern>}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af10\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\sb140\sa120\keepn\f3\fs28\b\dbch\af7\ql\sb140\sa120\ltrpar{\loch
